  "interpretation": [
    "One instrumented Linux static slow call spent 9.354 ms of 11.484 ms in the voice batch; summed voice wall time exceeded summed voice CPU time by about 8.341 ms.",
    "One instrumented Linux pose slow call spent 16.231 ms of 21.654 ms in the late-field stage. The driver CPU interval does not include other worker threads, so this does not identify the cause of the late-field delay.",
    "For those calls, worker_roundtrip minus worker_execution was about 0.065/0.057 ms; most time was inside the owned worker job rather than its external handoff.",
    "These instrumented calls are new observations, not causal identification of the prior four unprofiled misses."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "Wall/CPU sums across parallel workers and nested stages cannot be added as exclusive CPU totals.",
    "CPU clocks do not distinguish OS descheduling, blocking, or waiting for another worker on their own.",
    "Diagnostics perturb timing and memory and are excluded from capacity acceptance.",
    "The identical Linux baseline binary measured differently across sessions; only within-session interleaved comparisons are used for candidate decisions.",
    "128/512-bin interpolation and two-item scheduling experiments did not provide stable overall benefit and were reverted.",
    "No new real-device long-stability acceptance is claimed. Existing zero-deadline-miss acceptance remains unmet."
  ],
